 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "The limit is decided in `Request.max_content_length` (`src/tessel/wrappers.py:60-90`). It uses a per-request value if one is set, and otherwise falls back to the `MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH` config (default `None`, set in `src/tessel/app.py:225`).\n\nIt can be changed per request. Assign to `request.max_content_length` in the view, before the body is accessed (e.g. before `request.files` or `request.form`):\n\n```python\n@app.post(\"/big-upload\")\ndef big_upload():\n    request.max_content_length = 100 * 1000 * 1000  # this route only\n    f = request.files[\"file\"]\n```\n\nPer-request setting was added in 3.1. If the 413 is raised for non-file form fields or too many parts, the analogous knobs are `request.max_form_memory_size` and `request.max_form_parts`.\n\nIf the global config is set low and you only want one route larger, set the config to the default limit and override on that route as above. A reverse proxy (e.g. nginx `client_max_body_size`) can also return a 413 before the app sees the request.",
